I think there's all these old school brands

2883
01:59:52.670 --> 01:59:54.520
that I'd like us to consider for ads.

2884
01:59:56.170 --> 01:59:58.270
It's broken and I have been talking about.

2885
01:59:59.250 --> 02:00:00.800
Oreos are vegan.

2886
02:00:00.800 --> 02:00:01.763
Come on, Oreos.

2887
02:00:02.890 --> 02:00:04.460
The under reported nutritional benefits

2888
02:00:04.460 --> 02:00:07.143
of pre packaged hostess products.

2889
02:00:09.210 --> 02:00:10.780
All right, Ted coaching.

2890
02:00:10.780 --> 02:00:11.880
Yes, Heidi.

2891
02:00:11.880 --> 02:00:14.270
I would say that,

2892
02:00:14.270 --> 02:00:15.699
I mean, I don't know,

2893
02:00:15.699 --> 02:00:16.865
you know, for me as a coach,

2894
02:00:16.865 --> 02:00:18.450
one of the first things that I,

2895
02:00:18.450 --> 02:00:20.390
if I'm gonna hire a coach,

2896
02:00:20.390 --> 02:00:22.940
so I've hired coaches for different events,

2897
02:00:22.940 --> 02:00:24.110
specific events.

2898
02:00:24.110 --> 02:00:25.750
I train myself pretty well,

2899
02:00:25.750 --> 02:00:28.740
but then if I'm doing like Ironman, I had a coach.

2900
02:00:28.740 --> 02:00:32.750
Kilimanjaro, I put together a team for that

2901
02:00:32.750 --> 02:00:34.770
just because I felt like I wanted to make sure

2902
02:00:34.770 --> 02:00:35.830
I had the right body stuff

2903
02:00:35.830 --> 02:00:38.070
and nutrition stuff and supplement stuff

2904
02:00:38.070 --> 02:00:40.602
and training and all that sort of thing.

2905
02:00:40.602 --> 02:00:45.170
I, as a coach, and also as an athlete,

2906
02:00:45.170 --> 02:00:47.860
I would like to know that someone

2907
02:00:47.860 --> 02:00:50.630
that I feel like someone can get me there.

2908
02:00:50.630 --> 02:00:52.530
I mean, it's as simple as that.

2909
02:00:52.530 --> 02:00:54.100
Can they get me there?

2910
02:00:54.100 --> 02:00:55.040
That's the first thing.

2911
02:00:55.040 --> 02:00:57.190
Is there a vibe, right?

2912
02:00:57.190 --> 02:00:59.060
Because you're gonna be spending some time with them,

2913
02:00:59.060 --> 02:01:00.646
there's gonna be conversations,

2914
02:01:00.646 --> 02:01:03.960
they're gonna be back and forth, email texts, workouts.

2915
02:01:03.960 --> 02:01:05.210
Do they understand you?

2916
02:01:05.210 --> 02:01:06.563
Do they not understand you?

2917
02:01:07.570 --> 02:01:12.570
I personally like someone who has had some experience,

2918
02:01:12.640 --> 02:01:15.450
I don't know, like they don't necessarily need

2919
02:01:15.450 --> 02:01:17.590
to have done the ultra man,

2920
02:01:17.590 --> 02:01:19.633
but some sort of.

2921
02:01:20.540 --> 02:01:23.270
Have they coached other athletes who have done that race?

2922
02:01:23.270 --> 02:01:25.940
Either that, or do they understand

2923
02:01:25.940 --> 02:01:27.890
what it's gonna take to get through it?

2924
02:01:27.890 --> 02:01:30.410
Meaning have they suffered a certain amount?

2925
02:01:30.410 --> 02:01:31.580
Do they understand what it's going

2926
02:01:31.580 --> 02:01:36.320
to take to recover from one day to the next right?

2927
02:01:36.320 --> 02:01:37.970
Cause it's a stage race

2928
02:01:37.970 --> 02:01:41.450
versus a 24 or 48 hour non-stop race.

2929
02:01:41.450 --> 02:01:44.530
So I think those kinds of questions,

2930
02:01:44.530 --> 02:01:47.770
but I think ultimately have had some experience?

2931
02:01:47.770 --> 02:01:50.140
Is the vibe there for you?

2932
02:01:50.140 --> 02:01:52.830
And do you think that they can actually get you there?

2933
02:01:52.830 --> 02:01:54.670
You know, I talked to a guy recently

2934
02:01:54.670 --> 02:01:58.040
who tried to climb Everest and didn't make it.

2935
02:01:58.040 --> 02:02:00.720
And he said that he thought it was his coach.

2936
02:02:00.720 --> 02:02:02.833
So that's either a, passing the buck,

2937
02:02:03.850 --> 02:02:06.530
or it's maybe the coach was not right,

2938
02:02:06.530 --> 02:02:08.920
maybe there was not the right vibe there.

2939
02:02:08.920 --> 02:02:12.020
So I think that it's an important relationship

2940
02:02:12.020 --> 02:02:15.573
when you take on a big event like that.

2941
02:02:17.035 --> 02:02:19.950
So that's what I would say.

2942
02:02:19.950 --> 02:02:21.190
I mean, I think that's all right.

2943
02:02:21.190 --> 02:02:23.750
I would agree with all of that on the vibe piece.

2944
02:02:23.750 --> 02:02:26.690
I think you need to be clear on what your needs are.

2945
02:02:26.690 --> 02:02:28.490
Like, do you need somebody to be

2946
02:02:28.490 --> 02:02:30.860
an emotional support for you

2947
02:02:30.860 --> 02:02:32.650
or do you just need the workouts?

2948
02:02:32.650 --> 02:02:36.220
Do you need feedback and what does that feedback look like?

2949
02:02:36.220 --> 02:02:37.580
Do you need emotional feedback?

2950
02:02:37.580 --> 02:02:39.820
Do you just need metrics feedback?

2951
02:02:39.820 --> 02:02:41.170
Do you like to be left alone?

2952
02:02:41.170 --> 02:02:43.530
Do you want somebody to tell you what to eat for breakfast?

2953
02:02:43.530 --> 02:02:45.750
Like all of that is gonna be different

2954
02:02:45.750 --> 02:02:47.180
depending upon the athlete.

2955
02:02:47.180 --> 02:02:48.013
And you wanna make sure

2956
02:02:48.013 --> 02:02:50.350
that you're in a good fit with a coach

2957
02:02:50.350 --> 02:02:53.530
who can meet the needs that you require,

2958
02:02:53.530 --> 02:02:56.100
but it requires clarity on what those needs are,

2959
02:02:56.100 --> 02:02:58.180
first of all, so you're not mismatched.

2960
02:02:58.180 --> 02:03:01.240
And I that's a good point

2961
02:03:01.240 --> 02:03:03.860
because there's so much that goes into,

2962
02:03:03.860 --> 02:03:06.810
see, I look at as a coach, you know,

2963
02:03:06.810 --> 02:03:10.423
I want someone to be getting body work done.

2964
02:03:10.423 --> 02:03:11.256
I want them to be more balanced.

2965
02:03:11.256 --> 02:03:14.960
I don't want it to just be metrics and numbers and speed.

2966
02:03:14.960 --> 02:03:18.130
It has to have nutrition has to happen properly.

2967
02:03:18.130 --> 02:03:20.050
Sleep has to happen properly.

2968
02:03:20.050 --> 02:03:22.550
So there is that and life happens.

2969
02:03:22.550 --> 02:03:25.640
So in any relationship in any event that we do,

2970
02:03:25.640 --> 02:03:27.840
stuff happens, we get sick,

2971
02:03:27.840 --> 02:03:30.390
kids go to school or they they're sick.

2972
02:03:30.390 --> 02:03:31.970
Is this coach gonna be understanding

2973
02:03:31.970 --> 02:03:34.963
of what the kind of gestalt of your life is?

2974
02:03:35.937 --> 02:03:37.650
And it depends on how deep it is.

2975
02:03:37.650 --> 02:03:39.180
Is it just a simple plan to say,

2976
02:03:39.180 --> 02:03:40.440
here's the plan, see you later?

2977
02:03:40.440 --> 02:03:42.770
Or is it actually going to be more

2978
02:03:42.770 --> 02:03:44.620
of an in-depth relationships?

2979
02:03:44.620 --> 02:03:48.585
And do you respond to positive feedback or negative?

2980
02:03:48.585 --> 02:03:50.070
Like, do you need somebody to say good job?

2981
02:03:50.070 --> 02:03:51.940
Or do you want somebody to say,

2982
02:03:51.940 --> 02:03:54.190
Hey, you're really like off the reservation here.

2983
02:03:54.190 --> 02:03:57.620
Are you gonna walk if they give you

2984
02:03:57.620 --> 02:03:59.411
some negative feedback?

2985
02:03:59.411 --> 02:04:00.780
Is that going to be a problem?

2986
02:04:00.780 --> 02:04:01.900
All of that is very personal.

2987
02:04:01.900 --> 02:04:03.830
And I think with respect to ultraman,

2988
02:04:03.830 --> 02:04:05.970
as somebody who's done Ultraman a couple of times,

2989
02:04:05.970 --> 02:04:08.020
it's very different from ironman.

2990
02:04:08.020 --> 02:04:11.886
So most people that coach iron man athletes

2991
02:04:11.886 --> 02:04:15.380
most likely have not coached somebody for ultra man.

2992
02:04:15.380 --> 02:04:17.950
Ultra man is completely different, like Ted said,

2993
02:04:17.950 --> 02:04:19.200
it's a stage race.

2994
02:04:19.200 --> 02:04:21.500
It's fundamentally a cycling race,

2995
02:04:21.500 --> 02:04:26.180
more than anything with a couple appendages tagged onto it.

2996
02:04:26.180 --> 02:04:27.910
And the way that you train for it

2997
02:04:27.910 --> 02:04:29.250
is going to look very different

2998
02:04:29.250 --> 02:04:31.277
from the way that you train

2999
02:04:31.277 --> 02:04:32.110
for any other kind of triathlon.

3000
02:04:32.110 --> 02:04:34.130
You don't need to do any transition work,

3001
02:04:34.130 --> 02:04:36.040
you don't need to new brick work,

3002
02:04:36.040 --> 02:04:38.140
you don't really need to any kind of tempo

3003
02:04:38.140 --> 02:04:39.810
or speed work for the most part,

3004
02:04:39.810 --> 02:04:43.465
unless you're already super accomplished and you need,

3005
02:04:43.465 --> 02:04:46.780
to sort of hone that razor's edge.

3006
02:04:46.780 --> 02:04:50.400
So it depends upon your skill level at the time as well.

3007
02:04:50.400 --> 02:04:53.677
So finding somebody who can meet all of those needs,

3008
02:04:53.677 --> 02:04:56.220
I mean, it's a tall order, but very doable.

3009
02:04:56.220 --> 02:04:57.053
And I'm glad that you're looking for a coach,

3010
02:04:57.053 --> 02:04:58.340
'cause I think you should have a coach

3011
02:04:58.340 --> 02:05:00.000
for a race like this.

3012
02:05:00.000 --> 02:05:01.080
There is this temptation.

3013
02:05:01.080 --> 02:05:02.230
I've heard this, not just from you,

3014
02:05:02.230 --> 02:05:03.280
but from other people like.

3015
02:05:03.280 --> 02:05:05.280
Oh, I heard Courtney Dauwalter

3016
02:05:05.280 --> 02:05:06.990
and she's all about intuitive.

3017
02:05:06.990 --> 02:05:08.210
And it's like, you got to understand,

3018
02:05:08.210 --> 02:05:11.120
like she is, you know, an outlier,

3019
02:05:11.120 --> 02:05:14.400
like most people left to their own intuition

3020
02:05:14.400 --> 02:05:16.440
to train the way that they feel

3021
02:05:16.440 --> 02:05:19.840
are gonna lead themselves down a dark alleyway

3022
02:05:19.840 --> 02:05:21.189
and it ain't going to be good.

3023
02:05:21.189 --> 02:05:23.080
And she had plenty of coaching along the way.

3024
02:05:23.080 --> 02:05:24.380
She has foundation of that course.

3025
02:05:24.380 --> 02:05:25.213
Absolutely.

3026
02:05:26.448 --> 02:05:28.130
Is it a 10 kilometer open water swim

3027
02:05:28.130 --> 02:05:30.233
then like a couple of hundred on the bike.

3028
02:05:33.820 --> 02:05:35.720
You're going 90 on the bike the first day

3029
02:05:35.720 --> 02:05:38.370
and 171 on the bike the next day.

3030
02:05:38.370 --> 02:05:40.110
And then you got a little double marathon.

3031
02:05:40.110 --> 02:05:43.390
You got to run in there, but now it's all very doable.

3032
02:05:43.390 --> 02:05:45.002
That's hilarious.

3033
02:05:45.002 --> 02:05:45.835
That's the dessert.

3034
02:05:45.835 --> 02:05:47.920
My advice is to make sure they can do

3035
02:05:47.920 --> 02:05:52.253
that whistle without the pinkies in their lips.

3036
02:05:53.244 --> 02:05:55.980
I want a coach that can whistle me like that

3037
02:05:55.980 --> 02:05:59.273
and then wear a headband at all times on Zoom.

3038
02:06:01.374 --> 02:06:03.283
In the proper snorkel mask.

3039
02:06:05.134 --> 02:06:07.020
And do they make you wear

3040
02:06:07.020 --> 02:06:09.023
a swim mask slash snorkel?

3041
02:06:11.440 --> 02:06:13.760
All right, we'll do one more question.

3042
02:06:13.760 --> 02:06:17.510
And this one's for me and it's tailored specifically

3043
02:06:17.510 --> 02:06:18.950
to Ted since he's here.

3044
02:06:18.950 --> 02:06:20.210
And I think it's a question

3045
02:06:20.210 --> 02:06:22.420
that I think will be beneficial to a lot of people.

3046
02:06:22.420 --> 02:06:23.900
And it's basically just

3047
02:06:25.630 --> 02:06:30.200
about how you Ted see the role of yoga

3048
02:06:30.200 --> 02:06:33.190
in the context of being an athlete.

3049
02:06:33.190 --> 02:06:35.290
Like I often look at yoga

3050
02:06:35.290 --> 02:06:38.150
and wish that I had been an avid practitioner

3051
02:06:38.150 --> 02:06:41.090
of yoga when I was in my competitive swimming years

3052
02:06:41.090 --> 02:06:43.460
and understanding the benefits of that,

3053
02:06:43.460 --> 02:06:46.760
not just for kind of strength and balance and agility,

3054
02:06:46.760 --> 02:06:49.840
but also restorative and injury prevention.

3055
02:06:49.840 --> 02:06:52.720
And of course, the true benefit of it,

3056
02:06:52.720 --> 02:06:57.270
which is kind of spiritual awareness.

3057
02:06:57.270 --> 02:06:59.750
So how do you think about how yoga fits in

3058
02:06:59.750 --> 02:07:03.780
to being an athlete and performance specifically?

3059
02:07:03.780 --> 02:07:07.950
And how do you sort of talk about how you recommend yoga

3060
02:07:07.950 --> 02:07:11.463
for the kind of every day or weekend warrior athlete?

3061
02:07:13.669 --> 02:07:15.530
I recommend yoga

3062
02:07:15.530 --> 02:07:18.550
for the every day weekend warrior athletes,

3063
02:07:18.550 --> 02:07:21.100
you know, two to three times a week if they could,

3064
02:07:21.100 --> 02:07:24.510
but the truth is most people are like once a week,

3065
02:07:24.510 --> 02:07:25.610
and that's it.

3066
02:07:25.610 --> 02:07:27.770
And I almost see it as if

3067
02:07:27.770 --> 02:07:29.790
you were gonna go run once a week.

3068
02:07:29.790 --> 02:07:31.460
You could go for a jog once a week

3069
02:07:31.460 --> 02:07:34.190
and go slow and go two, three miles or four miles

3070
02:07:34.190 --> 02:07:35.620
or five miles once a week

3071
02:07:35.620 --> 02:07:39.010
is not really gonna get you to a marathon

3072
02:07:39.010 --> 02:07:40.280
if you're doing that.

3073
02:07:40.280 --> 02:07:43.130
So yoga, I think is a similar thing.

3074
02:07:43.130 --> 02:07:47.440
In my opinion, it is again, like I said earlier,

3075
02:07:47.440 --> 02:07:49.790
the glue that brings it all together.

3076
02:07:49.790 --> 02:07:52.360
The first class I ever took was Brian Kest,

3077
02:07:52.360 --> 02:07:54.010
back in Santa Monica, right?

3078
02:07:54.010 --> 02:07:55.740
We used to go up the stairs

3079
02:07:56.580 --> 02:07:58.110
and then there'd be like a little chest

3080
02:07:58.110 --> 02:08:00.817
and you could just leave whatever money you wanted.

3081
02:08:00.817 --> 02:08:02.317
There was like donation-based.

3082
02:08:06.337 --> 02:08:10.020
So that day I fell in love with yoga because it was,

3083
02:08:10.020 --> 02:08:12.780
as an athlete growing up, playing baseball,

3084
02:08:12.780 --> 02:08:15.900
and football and lacrosse back on the east coast.

3085
02:08:15.900 --> 02:08:18.670
I started that and I was sore for four days

3086
02:08:18.670 --> 02:08:20.297
and I couldn't believe it

3087
02:08:20.297 --> 02:08:21.575
and I could barely hold my body up.

3088
02:08:21.575 --> 02:08:24.140
And I thought, wow, this is real, first of all.

3089
02:08:24.140 --> 02:08:26.440
And it just made me feel so good

3090
02:08:26.440 --> 02:08:29.103
and just having stress in life and,

3091
02:08:30.068 --> 02:08:32.550
I was at that time.

3092
02:08:32.550 --> 02:08:35.075
I dunno how sober I was.

3093
02:08:35.075 --> 02:08:36.070
It was maybe a few years, right?

3094
02:08:36.070 --> 02:08:38.183
So it was just a sales still stressful.

3095
02:08:39.610 --> 02:08:43.150
And it was a big sigh of relief for me.

3096
02:08:43.150 --> 02:08:45.470
And every single class that I went to

3097
02:08:45.470 --> 02:08:47.560
was a big sigh of relief

3098
02:08:47.560 --> 02:08:51.460
and then I started doing more.

3099
02:08:51.460 --> 02:08:54.520
So I did that for almost three years, just yoga.

3100
02:08:54.520 --> 02:08:56.153
Then I started running,

3101
02:08:56.153 --> 02:08:58.196
I thought, oh, I want a little cardio in my life.

3102
02:08:58.196 --> 02:09:00.608
So I'm gonna add a couple miles a couple of times a week

3103
02:09:00.608 --> 02:09:03.230
and ran two miles and was sore for four days

3104
02:09:03.230 --> 02:09:05.430
because I didn't run for almost three years.

3105
02:09:06.280 --> 02:09:08.920
Then started to run again

3106
02:09:08.920 --> 02:09:13.220
and realized how much the yoga practice actually helped me

3107
02:09:13.220 --> 02:09:15.620
just balance out my body.

3108
02:09:15.620 --> 02:09:19.330
So from a physical standpoint, in my opinion,

3109
02:09:19.330 --> 02:09:23.760
I think that it is absolutely 100% necessary

3110
02:09:23.760 --> 02:09:26.140
because from an athletic standpoint,

3111
02:09:26.140 --> 02:09:28.130
you're just pounding and pounding and pounding and pounding

3112
02:09:28.130 --> 02:09:30.455
and trying to get faster and stronger

3113
02:09:30.455 --> 02:09:31.288
and faster and stronger, faster and stronger.

3114
02:09:31.288 --> 02:09:34.410
And there's not really a sense.

3115
02:09:34.410 --> 02:09:37.770
I mean, now in the last maybe decade,

3116
02:09:37.770 --> 02:09:40.870
there's been a lot more attention to recovery,

3117
02:09:40.870 --> 02:09:45.430
but in my opinion, yoga is definitely something

3118
02:09:45.430 --> 02:09:47.120
that people should be doing on a regular basis.

3119
02:09:47.120 --> 02:09:50.480
Now, obviously the word yoga is such a huge umbrella.

3120
02:09:50.480 --> 02:09:52.640
So what I would recommend is

3121
02:09:52.640 --> 02:09:54.580
one or two classes a week,

3122
02:09:54.580 --> 02:09:56.630
that's a little bit more of a flow style

3123
02:09:56.630 --> 02:10:00.660
and at least one, or maybe two classes a week, that's yin.

3124
02:10:00.660 --> 02:10:02.860
Because sitting in those poses for a really long time

3125
02:10:02.860 --> 02:10:04.500
and lengthening your connective tissue,

3126
02:10:04.500 --> 02:10:05.950
I think has a huge benefit.

3127
02:10:05.950 --> 02:10:07.380
I feel like that's one of the reasons

3128
02:10:07.380 --> 02:10:10.540
why I've been able to keep my flexibility,

3129
02:10:10.540 --> 02:10:13.870
even though I'll do endurance events still.

3130
02:10:13.870 --> 02:10:15.540
So from a physical standpoint,

3131
02:10:15.540 --> 02:10:16.590
I think that's a big thing.

3132
02:10:16.590 --> 02:10:20.076
I think that, back when I was adventure racing,

3133
02:10:20.076 --> 02:10:23.710
2001 through five basically

3134
02:10:23.710 --> 02:10:26.090
is kind of my four or five year stint

3135
02:10:26.090 --> 02:10:26.970
in adventure races

3136
02:10:26.970 --> 02:10:29.310
and anything from two to five hour sprint races

3137
02:10:29.310 --> 02:10:31.500
all the way up to 24 to 48 hour races.

3138
02:10:31.500 --> 02:10:35.360
And I remember passing team balanced bar

3139
02:10:35.360 --> 02:10:37.710
